    "path": "/corrections/0/finding",
    "change": "changed",
    "new": "The question asks when Rachel may draw, the hand condition and card type, and whether a faceup emergency prevents it. It does not ask the draw amount. The map currently includes one action as part of its asked fact. This is the same quantity-versus-trigger distinction applied to the resolved payment finding."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/0/material_required_scope",
    "change": "added",
    "new": "End of every deal including another player's, owner hand has zero actions, optional draw of owner sheet's topmost type, emergency outside hand does not prevent it."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/0/correct_unasked_context",
    "change": "added",
    "new": "The fixed ability draws one action. A volunteered claim of two would still contradict the fixed key."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/0/proposed_versioned_correction",
    "change": "changed",
    "new": "In a future clause-map/key scope version, move the one-card quantity into context; retain all timing, zero-hand condition, optionality, owner/type and emergency treatment. Alternatively make the question explicitly ask how many; do not silently enlarge frozen wording."
  },
