    "path": "/corrections/1/finding",
    "change": "changed",
    "new": "The final Jackson clause asks what produces the capital payment, which asks its condition. It does not ask how much is paid. The map includes gains two capital as an asked requirement, although activation cost is separately the exhaust cost."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/1/material_required_scope",
    "change": "added",
    "new": "Predict when the asset is revealed, optional exhaust, another player rather than self, payment to Jackson user if the selected player wins the deal."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/1/correct_unasked_context",
    "change": "added",
    "new": "The fixed payment is two capital. A volunteered wrong amount remains a material contradiction."
  },
  {
    "path": "/corrections/1/proposed_versioned_correction",
    "change": "changed",
    "new": "In a future clause-map/key scope version, put the two-capital payment quantity in context and require the selected-player-win condition and recipient. Alternatively explicitly ask the payment amount in a new question version. Preserve the asked exhaust activation cost."
